"""layers.0.mlp.down_proj:2648 -- a word detector for "data", "high" and "series".

This component sits in the first layer, so its activation is almost entirely a
function of the current token's identity (about two thirds of its variance is
explained in-sample by which token it is; the context hardly matters). It is
strongly positive on the word "data" (in any case or spelling: data, Data, DATA,
.data, _data, (data) and the Chinese 数据), on "high" (High, high), and on
"series" (series, Series, 系列). It is moderately positive
on a few other word families: higher/highest, family and royalty words
(girl, king, queen, brother; Chinese 妹 姐 弟 哥 王 君 男 女孩), common
Chinese nouns that close a compound name (版 号 网 机 车 房 城 村 港 队 ...),
and a handful of English modifiers (new, next, low, free, special, health,
international, extra). Everything else is near zero.

The program is stateless: it looks only at the newest token, which is the
token whose activation it predicts.
"""

READS = ()

DATA = {"data"}                                            # English 'data' in any case
DATA_CN = {"数据", "的数据"}                                  # 'data' in Chinese
HIGH = {"high"}
HIGHER = {"higher", "highest"}
SERIES = {"series"}                                         # English 'series'
SERIES_CN = {"系列", "系"}                                   # 'series' in Chinese
PEOPLE_EN = {"girl", "girls", "boy", "king", "kings", "queen", "prince",
             "princess", "brother", "brothers"}
PEOPLE_CN = {"妹", "姐", "弟", "哥", "王子", "王", "君", "男", "女孩"}
SUFFIX_CN = set("版号號网網机機车房城村港队隊篇草菜班鞋袜衣货套")
MODIFIERS_EN = {"new", "next", "low", "free", "extra", "special", "health", "international"}


def _word(token: str) -> str:
    """The token as a bare word: no leading space, no punctuation, lower case."""
    return token.strip().lower().strip("._$(/-\"'")


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    token = prefix.token_strings[-1]
    word = _word(token)
    if word in DATA or token in DATA_CN:
        return carry, 0.74
    if word == "high":
        return carry, 0.67
    if word in HIGHER:
        return carry, 0.25
    if word in SERIES or token in SERIES_CN:
        return carry, 0.5
    if word in PEOPLE_EN:
        return carry, 0.17
    if token in PEOPLE_CN:
        return carry, 0.4
    if token in SUFFIX_CN:
        return carry, 0.41
    if word in MODIFIERS_EN:
        return carry, 0.16
    return carry, 0.0

