"""A detector for the start of parenthetical, quoted, or symbolic material.
An ASCII space before an opening parenthesis is the strongest cue. It is
stronger after a word/identifier than after numbers, operators, or whitespace.
Other opening delimiters, quote markers, and double underscores give smaller
responses. Joined empty parentheses and newline-ending braces are suppressed.
Small auxiliary rules cover LaTeX's frac and spaced East Asian characters.
This is a surface-form approximation, not a parser: it remembers only the
previous token and clears that context at document boundaries.
