"""A lexical love/affection signal, not sentence-level sentiment.
Chinese love characters respond most strongly; compounds, English love
inflections, and love words in other languages respond less strongly.
Related liking, emotional attachment, and care words have weak responses.
Selected traditional Chinese spellings are normalized, with a smaller
response for compounds containing traditional 愛. Completed byte-split 爱
is recognized too, with a response depending on how its bytes were split.
Otherwise unlisted tokens get zero; sentence sentiment is not inferred.
